{"archetypes":[{"name":"sequence-absorb","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan absorbs SKILL.md Step 0 calls #10–#16 into phase_plan_materialize and explicitly names order-of-operations divergence as a primary failure mode; a reviewer must verify the plan's stated sequence matches the source SKILL.md blocks being replaced.","prompt_body":"Audit the plan's stated operation order inside phase_plan_materialize (snapshot → gh-compose → copy-plan → workflow-path → persist-run-flags → dirty-tree → slug/branch → git-current-branch → plan-log → larch:plan-summary) against the current SKILL.md Step 0 blocks claimed for absorption at L645–810, checking for any reordering, skipped steps, or operations that cross a phase boundary they should not. Check that the bail-on-first-failure guarantee is preserved: persist-run-flags must execute before dirty-tree, and dirty-tree must execute before branch creation, matching SKILL.md's original sequencing intent. Verify that the snapshot-untracked.sh baseline write is placed at function entry (the position between SKILL.md call #9 and #10) rather than after branch creation, where it would corrupt the baseline semantics relied on by check-review-changes.sh. Confirm that the plan's prose description of the function body is internally consistent with the sequence documented in its own Failure Modes section 1. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"kv-tail-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds three new KV tail keys (BRANCH_NAME, BRANCH_ACTION, PLAN_FILE) and two breadcrumbs to emit_final_tail; cross-doc consistency between the plan's emission spec and the downstream SKILL.md KV consumers has not been independently validated.","prompt_body":"Check that every KV key the plan adds to emit_final_tail (BRANCH_NAME, BRANCH_ACTION, PLAN_FILE) is actually consumed by the SKILL.md KV parsing block and that no downstream variable assignments silently receive empty strings on the paths where the plan states the keys are populated. Verify that the two breadcrumb strings ('→ step0: branch $BRANCH_NAME + plan logged' and '→ step0: larch:plan posted') exactly match the strings documented in implement-bootstrap.md's breadcrumbs section and are not displaced by prior-phase breadcrumbs. Examine whether the plan's claim that BRANCH_ACTION is empty on IS_USER_BRANCH and FORKED_TARGET skip paths is consistent with any conditional logic in SKILL.md that reads BRANCH_ACTION, and whether an empty BRANCH_ACTION on those paths is safe for all consumers. Check that the plan's promise to preserve existing empty placeholder keys for parser stability is actually honored in the emit_final_tail update rather than introducing new uninitialized globals that could silently break the current SKILL.md KV consumers when phase_plan_materialize's bail paths do not set them. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-gap","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan prescribes test cases B5–B10 but the Edge Cases section explicitly defers multiple failure paths (empty title, cp failure, gh auth failure); a reviewer must verify the test set covers the plan's own stated edge cases and that deferrals cannot cause silent runtime failures.","prompt_body":"Audit test cases B5–B10 against every named edge case and failure mode in the plan's Edge Cases and Failure Modes sections, flagging any acknowledged edge case that is deferred without a rationale for why the deferral cannot produce a silent runtime failure. Specifically check whether the deferred empty-title slug path can produce a malformed branch name (leading slash or dash after the prefix delimiter) that breaks a downstream git operation without any test guard catching it first. Verify that the cp-failure path, resolved as STEP_FAILED=copy-plan plus exit 2 rather than a bail reason, is either exercised by at least one B-case or its omission is explicitly scoped out in the test file with a comment. Check that the plan's extension of B2-plan and B4-plan to assert no new bail reasons overwrite prior tracking bail reasons is concretely specified in the test changes section rather than only mentioned discursively in the Failure Modes discussion, and confirm B10 (missing --preflight-tmpdir) covers the post-parse validation block rather than only the missing-arg detection. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
